Bugfix: Add a skip link to the signed-in layout

The signed-in layout had no skip link. Five tab stops separated the start of
every page from its first content element - the logo, the app menu toggle,
the search box, the user menu and the burger button nested inside the app
menu toggle - and they repeated on every page a keyboard user opened.

A skip link had existed once before. It was introduced in December 2014 and
removed five days later, because the focus did not move into the content when
the link was activated. Its CSS scaffold stayed behind in header.css as dead
code and shipped with every page for over ten years.

The scaffold is in use again. The link is the first tab stop of the page and
moves the focus into the main region, which tabindex="-1" on the content
element now allows. The focus style was corrected for today's teal header,
where the original white label text would have reached 1.61:1.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 2.4.1